date-released: "2026-11-14"
keywords:
  - 3D Gaussian Splatting
  - dynamic scene mapping
  - probability calibration
  - evidence pooling
  - reproducibility
abstract: >-
  Mechanism study on source-aware evidence pooling for dynamic Gaussian mapping.
  Separates a statistical problem (derived cues reusing the same measurements create
  confidence without new information) from a mapping problem (dynamic-pixel suppression
  via static initialization plus a masked rendering loss). Mapping experiments use oracle
  poses, depth and masks and are mechanism-level evidence, not end-to-end SLAM results.
